---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";

const updated = "November 2, 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy | GridFlow"
  description="How the GridFlow website handles your information: no cookies, no tracking, and email only when you write to us."
  darkHeader
>
  <PageHeader title="Privacy" lede={`Last updated ${updated}`} />

  <section class="policy">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="intro">
        This page explains what information the GridFlow website collects and how we use it. The short version: we don't
        track you, and we only have your information if you choose to email us.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        This website is run by GridFlow Inc., based in Albuquerque, New Mexico. You can reach us at
        <a href="mailto:info@gridflow.tech">info@gridflow.tech</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p>
        This website doesn't use cookies, analytics, advertising pixels or any other tracking tools. It doesn't store
        anything in your browser, and it doesn't load content from social media or ad networks. If we ever add tools like
        these, we'll update this page first.
      </p>

      <h2>Information you send us</h2>
      <p>
        When you email us, for example about a project, a job or investing, we receive whatever you include, such as your
        name, email address and message. We use it only to reply to you and follow up on what you asked about. We don't
        sell or rent your information, and we only share it when we need to in order to respond to you or when the law
        requires it.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you'd like us to delete your messages or information, email
        <a href="mailto:info@gridflow.tech">info@gridflow.tech</a> and we'll take care of it.
      </p>

      <h2>Website hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted by GitHub. Like most web hosts, GitHub may log basic technical information such as IP addresses
        to keep the service secure and running. GitHub handles that information under its own
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener"
          >privacy statement</a
        >. We don't use these logs to identify visitors.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>
        We link to other websites, such as news articles and LinkedIn profiles. Once you leave our site, that site's own
        privacy policy applies.
      </p>

      <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>This website is meant for a general business audience. We don't knowingly collect information from children.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this page</h2>
      <p>
        If how we handle information changes, we'll update this page and the date at the top. Questions? Email
        <a href="mailto:info@gridflow.tech">info@gridflow.tech</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .policy {
    padding-block: clamp(56px, 8vw, 96px) var(--section);
  }
  .intro {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .prose h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.375rem, 2.2vw, 1.75rem);
    margin-top: 48px;
  }
  .prose p {
    margin-top: 14px;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
</style>
